  parameters in config/arm_params.yaml, converted to metres):

      pivot_radius    t  =  45 mm   shoulder pivot lines (actuation joints)
      upper_arm_len  rf = 160 mm   upper arm  (revolute, actuated)
      rod_len        re = 320 mm   lower rod  (ball joint at BOTH ends)
      ee_radius      pr =  60 mm   platform circumradius (apex-down, hanging

  each platform joint sits on the SAME radial as its actuation joint):

      arm joints: (0,-45,0)  (38.97,22.5,0)  (-38.97,22.5,0)
      platform joints:      (0,-60,0) (51.96,30,0) (-51.96,30,0)

  Servos are mounted UNDER the base plate at servo_radius = 150 mm, matching
  the visualiser's servo+parallelogram interlinkage (servo_z < 0). The motor
  boxes at radius t mark the actuation joints the plugin actually servoes.

  Closed kinematic loops: each leg ends in a BALL joint into the shared
  platform link (SDF ball joints - impossible in plain URDF). The
  delta_arm_gazebo_plugin subscribes to arm/motor_targets (degrees) and
